            "id": "excalidraw-q1",
            "repoId": "excalidraw",
            "text": "When a user drags a container element that has bound arrows or text, how does Excalidraw propagate the position update to those bound elements — which function computes the new binding-aware endpoint position for a bound arrow, and which separate function applies that computed point to actually move the arrow?",
            "category": "GRAPH_HEAVY",
            "goldFacts": [
                {
                    "id": "excalidraw-q1-f1",
                    "statement": "dragSelectedElements, for each non-arrow element being dragged, calls updateBoundElements(element, scene.getElementsMapIncludingDeleted(), { simultaneouslyUpdated: ... }) after moving the element's coordinates, to keep its bound elements attached.",
                    "evidence": "packages/excalidraw/element/dragElements.ts:102"
                },
                {
                    "id": "excalidraw-q1-f2",
                    "statement": "updateBoundElements returns immediately without doing anything if the changed element is not a bindable element (isBindableElement(changedElement) is false).",
                    "evidence": "packages/excalidraw/element/binding.ts:747"
                },
                {
                    "id": "excalidraw-q1-f3",
                    "statement": "updateBoundElements uses boundElementsVisitor to visit elements bound to the changed element, but the visitor callback itself skips (returns early for) any element that is not a non-deleted linear element, and separately skips any bound element that doesNeedUpdate reports as not stale — only the remaining elements are actually repositioned.",
                    "evidence": "packages/excalidraw/element/binding.ts:751"
                },
                {
                    "id": "excalidraw-q1-f4",
                    "statement": "updateBoundPoint(element, bindingProp, bindings[bindingProp], bindableElement, elementsMap) is the function that computes the new binding-aware endpoint position for a bound linear element's start or end point; it is called from inside the bindableElementsVisitor callback that builds the `updates` array.",
                    "evidence": "packages/excalidraw/element/binding.ts:810"
                },
                {
                    "id": "excalidraw-q1-f5",
                    "statement": "For a bound linear element that is not simultaneously being updated itself, updateBoundElements takes the point(s) already computed by updateBoundPoint (the `updates` array) and calls LinearElementEditor.movePoints(element, updates, ...) to actually apply them and move the arrow's bound point(s).",
                    "evidence": "packages/excalidraw/element/binding.ts:838"
                },
                {
                    "id": "excalidraw-q1-f6",
                    "statement": "If the bound linear element also has a bound text label, updateBoundElements calls handleBindTextResize(element, elementsMap, false) to keep that label positioned correctly after the reposition.",
                    "evidence": "packages/excalidraw/element/binding.ts:849"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "excalidraw-q2",
            "repoId": "excalidraw",
            "text": "When elements are deleted from the scene (e.g. via the Delete/Backspace action), how does Excalidraw clean up the bindings that referenced those now-deleted elements, so that surviving elements don't keep dangling references to elements that no longer exist?",
            "category": "GRAPH_HEAVY",
            "goldFacts": [
                {
                    "id": "excalidraw-q2-f1",
                    "statement": "actionDeleteSelected's perform, after deleteSelectedElements produces the next element list, calls fixBindingsAfterDeletion(nextElements, nextElements.filter((el) => el.isDeleted)) to clean up bindings that referenced the just-deleted elements.",
                    "evidence": "packages/excalidraw/actions/actionDeleteSelected.tsx:275"
                },
                {
                    "id": "excalidraw-q2-f2",
                    "statement": "fixBindingsAfterDeletion, for each deleted element, calls BoundElement.unbindAffected(elements, element, mutateElement) to strip that deleted element's id out of the boundElements list of any bindable element (e.g. a container or arrow endpoint) it had been attached to.",
                    "evidence": "packages/excalidraw/element/binding.ts:1526"
