            "costUsd": null,
            "finalAnswer": "When a container element with bound arrows or text is dragged in Excalidraw, the position updates for those bound elements are propagated as follows:\n\n1. The function that computes the new binding-aware endpoint position for a bound arrow is `updateBoundPoint` in the file `packages/excalidraw/element/binding.ts`. This function calculates the new position of a bound point on the arrow as the container moves.\n\n2. The function that applies the computed binding-aware point to actually move the arrow is `LinearElementEditor.movePoints` located in `packages/excalidraw/element/linearElementEditor.ts`. This function takes the updated points and applies them to the arrow element, updating its position accordingly.\n\nThis flow is orchestrated in the function `updateBoundElements` (also in `binding.ts`), which:\n- Iterates over the bound elements of a changed element (like the dragged container).\n- Uses `updateBoundPoint` to compute new binding points for bound arrows.\n- Applies these computed points using `LinearElementEditor.movePoints`.\n\nSummary:\n- Compute new binding-aware endpoint position: `updateBoundPoint`\n- Apply the new binding-aware point to move the arrow: `LinearElementEditor.movePoints`\n\nThese functions together ensure that when a container is moved, all bound arrows update their endpoint positions accurately relative to the moved container.",
