            "wallClockMillis": 206630,
            "costUsd": null,
            "finalAnswer": "An element in the scene is drawn onto the canvas by the React component `StaticCanvas` (defined in `packages/excalidraw/components/canvases/StaticCanvas.tsx`). This component receives a canvas and a RoughCanvas instance among its props and calls the `renderStaticScene` function from `packages/excalidraw/renderer/staticScene.ts` inside a React `useEffect`.\n\nThe `renderStaticScene` function handles the rendering of the visible elements on the canvas. It calls an internal function `_renderStaticScene`, which iterates over each visible element and invokes the `renderElement` function for each one to paint it on the canvas.\n\nThe `renderElement` function (located in `packages/excalidraw/renderer/renderElement.ts`) is responsible for drawing a single element. For most element types (like rectangle, diamond, ellipse, line, arrow, image, text, iframe, embeddable), it obtains or generates the roughjs shape by calling `ShapeCache.generateElementShape`. This function manages caching and calls the core shape generator `_generateElementShape` in `packages/excalidraw/scene/Shape.ts`.\n\n`_generateElementShape` uses the roughjs generator to create the roughjs drawable shape based on the element's specific properties (such as points, width, height, roundness, arrowheads, etc.). It uses helper functions like `generateRoughOptions` to generate styling options for roughjs.\n\nSummary:\n- React component `StaticCanvas` invokes `renderStaticScene`.\n- `renderStaticScene` calls `_renderStaticScene`.\n- `_renderStaticScene` calls `renderElement` for each visible element.\n- `renderElement` calls `ShapeCache.generateElementShape` to get or generate the roughjs shape.\n- `ShapeCache.generateElementShape` calls `_generateElementShape` which uses roughjs generator methods to create the shape to draw on canvas.\n\nThis is how the roughjs shape for each element is obtained/generated for rendering on the canvas.",
